from pathlib import Path
import numpy as np,json
import matplotlib
matplotlib.use('Agg')
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt
O=Path(__file__).parent;a=np.load(O/'force-yaw-fit.npz');b=np.load(O/'force-yaw-conditioned-fit.npz');j=json.loads((O/'force-yaw-fit.json').read_text());f,axs=plt.subplots(4,3,figsize=(13,11),sharex=True)
for col,i in enumerate([0,2,5]):
 day,start=j['validation_windows'][i];data=np.load(O/(day+'-physical-input.npz'));force=np.load(O/(day+'-force-state.npz'));idx=np.searchsorted(data['t'],start);v=data['Y'][idx:idx+76,6:9]-force['wind'][idx:idx+76];axs[0,col].plot(a['t'],np.linalg.norm(v[:,:2],axis=1),'k');axs[0,col].axhline(np.linalg.norm(v[0,:2]),ls=':',color='tab:blue');axs[0,col].set(title=f'{day}, {start} s',ylabel='Inferred horizontal\nairspeed (m/s)')
 for row,k in enumerate([1,0,2],1):
  ax=axs[row,col];ax.plot(a['t'],np.rad2deg(a['truth'][i,:,k]),'k',lw=2,label='Recorded / reconstructed');ax.plot(a['t'],np.rad2deg(a['model'][i,:,k]),label='Constant initial speed');ax.plot(b['t'],np.rad2deg(b['model'][i,:,k]),label='Measured speed + vertical force');ax.set(ylabel=['Force tilt (deg)','Payload bank (deg)','Heading change (deg)'][row-1])
 for ax in axs[:,col]:ax.grid(alpha=.2)
 axs[-1,col].set_xlabel('Replay time (s)')
axs[1,0].legend(fontsize=7);f.suptitle('Yaw coupling and changing speed: useful diagnostics, still an inadequate turn model');f.tight_layout();f.savefig(O/'iteration-force-yaw-speed.png',dpi=160)
p=O/'physics-development.html';s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8-sig');s=s.replace('</html>','''<section id="force-yaw-speed"><h2>Yaw coupling and speed changes do not close the gap</h2><p>A reduced model now predicts effective force tilt, suspended-payload bank, heading rate and heading-minus-air-course together. It is fitted to the existing 316 three-second training windows, balanced across flight and manual/assisted groups. The development turns and five quarantined Trout Lake blocks are excluded from training. The heading-minus-course angle is a horizontal mismatch, not a direct measurement of canopy sideslip.</p><pre>s = ψ − χ
χ̇ = g tan(λ) / V_horizontal
ṡ = ψ̇ − χ̇
λ̇ = Kδ scale δ_filtered − Kλ sin λ + Kr ψ̇ + Ks sin s + Kp φ̇ + B throttle
ψ̈ = Ky scale δ_filtered − Dy (ψ̇ − χ̇) − Ky_s sin s</pre><p>The free diagnostic holds initial inferred horizontal airspeed constant and assumes vertical specific force near g. A separately refitted conditional version receives measured horizontal speed and vertical specific force throughout the interval, replacing g in the course equation. It therefore tests the longitudinal assumption but cannot be used as a simulator. Payload bank retains the previous second-order response to force direction.</p><figure><img src="iteration-force-yaw-speed.png" alt="Speed, force tilt, bank and heading comparisons for yaw-coupled and speed-conditioned models"><figcaption>Black: flight data and reconstructed quantities. Blue: free prediction with fixed initial speed. Orange: diagnostic supplied future speed and vertical-force measurements. Inferred horizontal speed uses the existing wind estimates; no pitot measurement is available.</figcaption></figure><p>The speed-conditioned version improves Hood River at 447 seconds: force-tilt RMS error falls from 15.35 to 8.89 degrees and bank error from 18.06 to 11.29 degrees. It still misses the turn substantially and worsens the early Trout Lake 402-second case. The separately tested first-order aerodynamic rate scaling proportional to speed, instead of dynamic-pressure/mass scaling, also fails to resolve the development errors. These fits are rejected; neither yaw coupling nor measured longitudinal motion alone is a sufficient correction to this reduced response law.</p><p>Several coefficients approach bounds, including weak force restoring and a near-zero direct brake term in the yaw-rate equation. These are symptoms of this fitted structure and dataset, not evidence that the actual canopy lacks brake-induced yaw. Evidence: <code>force-yaw-fit.json</code>, <code>force-yaw-conditioned-fit.json</code>, <code>force-yaw-rate-scaled-fit.json</code>. Code: <code>force_yaw.cpp</code>, <code>fit_force_yaw.py</code> and their named diagnostic variants. No production simulator changes have been made.</p></section></html>''');p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
